# What must not enter the build context.
#
# Two entries here are about correctness rather than about image size.
#
# `.env` is first because it is the one that costs something. It is gitignored, so it never reaches
# a commit — but `COPY . .` would put a developer's real database URL and approver token into an
# image layer, where `docker history` will show it for as long as the image exists. Nothing in this
# repository copies the whole directory today; this line is here for the day something does.
#
# `data/generated/` is excluded because the image regenerates the corpus from its committed seed in
# the build stage. Shipping a locally generated corpus into the context would mean the image was
# built from whatever happened to be on the builder's disk, and the seed would stop being the thing
# that decides what the corpus is.
#
# `.fastembed_cache/` is excluded for the same reason in miniature: the build stage downloads the
# model it was measured with, and a local cache that had drifted to another model would be used in
# preference without anything saying so.

.env
.venv/
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
data/generated/
.fastembed_cache/
docs/screenshots/
node_modules/
.claude/

# Not excluded, deliberately: artifacts/. The evidence screen reads those files and is the one
# screen that works with no database, so they belong in the image.
